  "narrative": "The conditional feature_027 tests are strong and scientifically informative: feature_027=1 remains associated with lower outcome_001 within feature_037=0, feature_002=0, feature_010=0, and even the stratum where all three accepted markers are absent (signed estimates 0.745-0.817, all lower bounds far above the 0.15 threshold). This argues against feature_027 being a simple proxy for the accepted trio within this supplied dataset, and I accept/close those conditional claims. The reciprocal tests also accept/close: feature_037=1, feature_002=1, and feature_010=1 retain large effects when feature_027 is absent (lower bounds above 0.328). These are conditional association statements in this dataset, not causal independence claims. feature_063 is the borderline case. Its direction is consistent across conditional strata, and two conditional claims cross the threshold (H112 in the triple-accepted-marker-absent stratum and H121 when feature_010 is absent), but they are near-threshold subgroup findings selected from multiple tests, while several adjacent conditional estimates fall just below threshold. I therefore keep the feature_063 conditional claims unresolved pending independent validation and request validation for the cleanest all-accepted-marker-absent claim, H112. If validation supports the threshold in that stratum, I will reassess H112 and consider H121 and the original H83; if strict independent uncertainty falls below threshold, I will close feature_063 as not sufficiently supported.",
